Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:54:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/18] B70: short research-note titles, strip note preamble,
 keep docs research on default budget

- Research-note titles now drop conversational lead-ins ("I'd like to",
  "Can you", "please"), the research verb and "the purchase of", use only
  the first sentence and cap at 10 words ("3D printer around $1000").
- The saved note (not the chat reply) drops a short model preamble such as
  "Receipt bound - 2 sources admitted. Here's the brief:".
- Fix from the regression run: requests that ask for primary or official
  sources are never treated as open-ended, so targeted documentation
  research keeps the default 3-search, 2-extract budget and immediate
  receipt. "Current best practices" had matched the open-ended detector.
  The 4 existing route tests that caught this now pass.

Research regression suites: 630 passed, 2 skipped. User-authorized on
2026-09-27.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
